            <ArticleTitle>A novel turn-on fluorescent probe for Al3+ and Fe3+ in aqueous solution and its imaging in living cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-262</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1386-1425(17)30888-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.saa.2017.11.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A quinoline-based fluorescence probe has been prepared and characterized. Probe 1 showed a selective sensing ability for Al3+ and Fe3+ ions through fluorescence enhancement response at 515nm when it was excited at 360nm. In the presence of Fe3+ ion, probe 1 exhibited a detection limit of 2.10×10-6M. As for Al3+, its detection limit of 3.58×10-7M was significantly lower than the highest limit of Al3+ in drinking water recommended by the WHO (7.41μM), representing a rare example in reported fluorescent probe for Al3+ ion. The fluorescence microscopy experiments have demonstrated that probe 1 could be used in live cells for the detection of Al3+ and Fe3+ ions.</AbstractText>
